# Frontend Rules

## Component Patterns

- Use **server components** by default for pages that fetch data
- Add `"use client"` only when the component needs interactivity (state, effects, event handlers)
- Group components by feature: `components/contributors/`, `components/chat/`, `components/dashboard/`
- Shared UI primitives live in `components/ui/` (shadcn-style) — check there before creating new base components

## Styling

- Use **Tailwind CSS v4** for all styling — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` to merge conditional class names
- Design tokens are defined in `src/styles/globals.css` under `@theme inline` — use CSS variables, not hardcoded colors
- Use the existing glass utility classes for card-like surfaces: `.glass`, `.glass-card`, `.glass-interactive`, `.glass-btn`
- The project supports light and dark mode — always ensure both work

## State Management

- Use **React Query** (via tRPC) for server data fetching and caching
- Use `useChat` from `@ai-sdk/react` for chat interactions
- Use local React hooks (`useState`, `useMemo`, `useCallback`) for UI state
- No Redux or Zustand — keep state simple and co-located

## Pages

- Pages are server components that fetch data directly using data-access or use-case functions
- Keep pages thin — delegate rendering to feature components
- Use loading.tsx and error.tsx for loading/error states when appropriate

## Avoid

- Don't create new base UI components without checking `src/components/ui/` first
- Don't use `fetch()` directly for internal API calls — use tRPC or server-side data-access functions
- Don't hardcode colors or spacing — use Tailwind tokens and CSS variables
- Don't import from barrel files if a direct import is available
